      "text": "Judson was established in the late 19th century as a mill village for the Camperdown Mills textile operations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/south-carolina_judson"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community of Judson is named after Adoniram Judson, a famous 19th-century American missionary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/south-carolina_judson"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Judson is located in west-central Greenville County near the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judson%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Judson is known for its proximity to the Swamp Rabbit Trail, a twenty-two mile multi-use greenway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
